From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:16:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat(documenteditor): Word-like backstage in the File
 menu

New ElixirChrome controller (app/elixir-chrome/) that extends the File
menu instance without changing FileMenu.js:

- Word order: Home, New, Open, Info | Save a Copy, Save As, Print,
  Share, Export, Close | Options. Open Recent, Rename, Protect, Version
  History, Access Rights and Go to Documents move to the pages that own
  them in Word (Open, Save As, Info, Share, Close). Fluent icons.
- Home (default page, like Word): greeting, New thumbnails (blank and
  the host templates) and the Recent list (name, location, date).
- Open: Recent with a filter box, Browse (upload through the host,
  editorConfig.elixir.uploadUrl) and the host start page.
- Info: Protect Document, Inspect Document (comments, tracked changes,
  personal information) and Version History tiles, the document
  properties in a column on the right.
- Save As: rename tile and the download formats as a list with
  descriptions; Export: Create PDF/PDF-A and Change File Type.
- Share: share with people (host sharing settings), copy or email a
  link (editorConfig.elixir.shareUrl), send a copy.
- Print: the browser picks the printer, copies and sides, so those
  rows give way to a note; Print button at the top like Word.

Strings in en, fr, de, es, it, pt, pt-pt, nl, ru, pl, ja, zh; other
locales fall back to English. The only hooks are the controller and
module declarations in app.js / app_dev.js and one less import.

[branding]

